invariant: INV-22
file: tcp_nonblocking_frame.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: tcp_nonblocking_fail names an alert for the caller to send after the
  peer's fatal alert, so a caller that follows ch_record_alert answers an
  alert that closed the connection, which RFC 9846 section 6.2 forbids.
  bin/tcp_nonblocking_loop_test requires ch_record_alert to read 0 after it,
  on both ends.

--- old
    r->alert = r->t.alert_received == 0 ? r->hs.alert : 0;
--- new
    r->alert = r->hs.alert;
